Package: inphDrugRepurposing
Title: Systems Biology Prioritizes Drug Candidates for Interferon-Activated
    Monocytes in Idiopathic Normal Pressure Hydrocephalus
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R:
    person("Masudul", "Haque", email = "masud.biochem.cu@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Reproducible computational workflow for identifying an
    interferon-activated classical-monocyte state in idiopathic normal
    pressure hydrocephalus (iNPH), deriving a 300-gene pseudobulk
    transcriptional signature, contextualizing that state against systemic
    lupus erythematosus, and prioritizing candidate compounds using LINCS
    L1000 transcriptional connectivity scoring. The project also includes
    leave-one-patient-out robustness analysis, a non-overlapping MSigDB
    Hallmark interferon-alpha pathway sensitivity analysis, figure
    generation, manuscript-number auditing, and table verification. The
    canonical 22,197-cell iNPH classical-monocyte analysis population is
    reconstructed from public GSE292141 raw count matrices using a
    version-controlled cell-membership manifest, together with documented
    public and external data resources.
